				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Source <a href="http://pagesix.com/2015/08/17/inside-madonnas-lavish-gypsy-themed-57th-birthday-bash/" target="_blank">Page Six</a>.</p>
<p><em><strong>Madonna</strong> threw a Spanish Gypsy-themed party at her Hamptons mansion on Sunday to celebrate her 57th birthday.</em></p>
<p><em>The Material Girl arrived “in a vintage Gypsy wagon filled to overflowing with dancers all in Gypsy attire” for the dance party in a tent filled with bales of hay on the grounds of her Bridgehampton home and 50-acre horse farm.</em></p>
<p><em>We’re told Madonna was escorted by a pair of handsome identical twins, Kevin and Jonathan Sampaio, and dancers from her upcoming “Rebel Heart” tour, who joined in a dance-off.</em></p>
<p><em>Guests including <strong>Naomi Watts</strong>, <strong>Kelly Ripa</strong> and <strong>Mark Consuelos</strong>, <strong>Andy Cohen</strong>, stylist <strong>B. Åkerlund</strong> and designers <strong>Jeremy Scott</strong> and <strong>Dan and Dean Caten</strong> came dressed in full Gypsy costume and were treated to a flamenco show.</em></p>
<p><em>The source added, “Everyone sat on the bales of hay and later stood on them to dance. The party was still going as the sun was rising on Monday morning.”</em></p>
<p><em>Madge’s kids — <strong>Lourdes, Rocco, David and Mercy</strong> — gave her a French bulldog puppy named Gypsy Rosa Lee for her birthday.</em></p>
