				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Madonna</strong> is living up to her nickname: the Material Girl tops <a href="http://www.forbes.com/sites/zackomalleygreenburg/2015/05/27/madonna-net-worth-in-2015-520-million/" target="_blank"><strong>Forbes</strong></a> annual list of the <strong>top-earning musicians</strong> by a wide margin.</p>
<p><strong>Madonna</strong> also claims the No. <strong>28</strong> spot on <strong>Forbes</strong> list of <strong>America’s Richest Self-Made Women</strong>, which appeared in the June 15th, 2015 issue of <a href="http://www.forbes.com/sites/zackomalleygreenburg/2015/05/27/madonna-net-worth-in-2015-520-million/" target="_blank">FORBES magazine</a>. She’s <strong>the wealthiest musician</strong> on the list.</p>
<p><strong>Queen of pop</strong>&#8216;s estimated net worth is <strong>$520 million</strong> (even if <a href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonna-richest-recording-artist/20141202" target="_blank">Wealth-X claims her worth is around $800m</a>); her sources are music, clothing and real estate.</p>
<p>Check out <strong>Forbes</strong> summary of the story:</p>
<p><em>One of the top pop divas of all time. Her tours have grossed an estimated $1.2 billion over the years, including $305 million from her 2012 MDNA tour. That helped her earn an estimated $125 million during the ensuing 12-month period during which FORBES calculated celebrity earnings, more than any other musician. Look for another bump when she goes on the road with her latest album, Rebel Heart, in August.</em></p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/forbes-madonna-is-the-wealthiest-musician/20150527">Forbes: &#8220;Madonna is the wealthiest musician.&#8221;</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
